{"builder":"Goal: one pull request that meets every one of these acceptance lines:\n- math.js exports clamp(x, lo, hi), which returns x limited to the range lo to hi\n- clamp(x, lo, hi) throws a RangeError when lo is greater than hi\n- README.md documents every function math.js exports\n- npm test passes\n\nContext (current repo): math.js is CommonJS and ends with `module.exports = { add, subtract, multiply };`. README.md has an `## API` section with `### add(a, b)` and `### multiply(a, b)` entries, each with a one-line description and a short js example. Note that `subtract` is exported but NOT documented in README.md today, so it must be added too. Tests live in test/math.test.js and run with `npm test` (`node --test`, Node 22).\n\nSteps:\n1. In math.js, add a function `clamp(x, lo, hi)` with a short doc comment like the others. If `lo > hi`, throw `new RangeError(...)` with a clear message (e.g. that lo must not be greater than hi). Otherwise return `Math.min(Math.max(x, lo), hi)`, so values below lo return lo, above hi return hi, and values inside the range (including exactly lo or hi) return x unchanged. lo === hi is a valid range and returns that value. Add `clamp` to `module.exports` and keep add, subtract and multiply exported unchanged.\n2. In README.md, under `## API`, add `### subtract(a, b)` (returns `a` minus `b`, with a small example) and `### clamp(x, lo, hi)` (returns `x` limited to the range `lo` to `hi`; throws a `RangeError` when `lo` is greater than `hi`; example such as `clamp(-5, 0, 100); // 0` and `clamp(140, 0, 100); // 100`). Use the same `### name(args)` heading style as the existing entries. Make sure every function exported from math.js has such an entry.\n3. In test/math.test.js, import clamp and add tests: value inside the range is unchanged; below lo returns lo; above hi returns hi; boundaries; lo === hi; `assert.throws(() => clamp(5, 10, 0), RangeError)`.\n4. Run these and make sure each succeeds before opening the PR:\n   - `npm test`\n   - `node -e \"const fs=require('fs');const m=require('./math.js');const r=fs.readFileSync('README.md','utf8');const missing=Object.keys(m).filter(k=>typeof m[k]==='function'&&!new RegExp('^#+\\\\s*\\`?'+k+'\\\\s*\\\\(','m').test(r));if(missing.length){console.log('MISSING: '+missing.join(', '));process.exit(1)}console.log('CHECK3 OK: '+Object.keys(m).join(', '))\"`\n5. Commit math.js, README.md and test/math.test.js and open one pull request describing the change and referencing https://github.com/o/r/issues/23.","verifier":"Check out the PR head and run every command from the repository root. There is one check per acceptance line, in order.\n\nCheck 1 — expect line: \"math.js exports clamp(x, lo, hi), which returns x limited to the range lo to hi\"\nRun:\n`node -e \"const m=require('./math.js');const a=require('node:assert/strict');a.equal(typeof m.clamp,'function');a.equal(m.clamp(5,0,10),5);a.equal(m.clamp(-5,0,100),0);a.equal(m.clamp(140,0,100),100);a.equal(m.clamp(0,0,100),0);a.equal(m.clamp(100,0,100),100);a.equal(m.clamp(7,7,7),7);a.equal(m.clamp(-3.5,-10,-1),-3.5);a.equal(m.clamp(-20,-10,-1),-10);console.log('CHECK1 OK')\"`\nPASS: it prints `CHECK1 OK` and exits 0. FAIL: any AssertionError, a TypeError (clamp missing or not a function), or a non-zero exit.\n\nCheck 2 — expect line: \"clamp(x, lo, hi) throws a RangeError when lo is greater than hi\"\nRun:\n`node -e \"const {clamp}=require('./math.js');const a=require('node:assert/strict');a.throws(()=>clamp(5,10,0),RangeError);a.throws(()=>clamp(0,1,0.5),RangeError);console.log('CHECK2 OK')\"`\nPASS: it prints `CHECK2 OK` and exits 0. FAIL: an AssertionError (nothing thrown, or an error that is not a RangeError) or a non-zero exit.\n\nCheck 3 — expect line: \"README.md documents every function math.js exports\"\nRun:\n`node -e \"const fs=require('fs');const m=require('./math.js');const r=fs.readFileSync('README.md','utf8');const missing=Object.keys(m).filter(k=>typeof m[k]==='function'&&!new RegExp('^#+\\\\s*\\`?'+k+'\\\\s*\\\\(','m').test(r));if(missing.length){console.log('MISSING: '+missing.join(', '));process.exit(1)}console.log('CHECK3 OK: '+Object.keys(m).join(', '))\"`\nThis lists every exported function and looks for a Markdown heading `name(` for it in README.md. Then open README.md and confirm each exported function listed (add, subtract, multiply, clamp, and any others) has an entry that describes what it does.\nPASS: every function exported by math.js is documented in README.md with a description (the script prints `CHECK3 OK` and your reading confirms it; if the script reports a name MISSING only because it is documented without a heading, read README.md and PASS if that function is clearly described there). FAIL: any exported function, e.g. `subtract` (undocumented before this change) or `clamp`, has no description in README.md.\n\nCheck 4 — expect line: \"npm test passes\"\nRun: `npm test`\nPASS: exit code 0 and the summary shows `# fail 0`. FAIL: non-zero exit or any failing test.\n\nAdvisory (not part of any PASS/FAIL condition):\n- Whether clamp(3, 2, 2) returns 2 without throwing (lo === hi should be a valid range).\n- Whether test/math.test.js gained tests for clamp, including the RangeError case.\n- Whether the README clamp entry mentions the RangeError behaviour."}